gpu_counters — Adreno perfcounter helper for SoloX

This directory contains a small, statically linked ARM64 helper that reads
Adreno hardware performance counters through /dev/kgsl-3d0.  It is pushed to
the tested device by solox/public/gpu_counters.py and executed through adb
shell; no root is required on ROMs that allow the shell user to access the
kgsl device node.

The ioctl numbers and structure layouts follow the Adreno kernel UAPI
(msm_kgsl.h).  They were cross-checked against google/hardware-perfcounter
(https://github.com/google/hardware-perfcounter, Apache-2.0), file
third_party/linux/adreno_driver_ioctl.h, which carries the original notice:

    SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note
    Copyright (c) 2018-2020, The Linux Foundation. All rights reserved.

The bandwidth counters match the VBIF/GBIF totals used by Snapdragon
Profiler's "GPU Memory Stats" (Read Total / Write Total):

    a7xx / a8xx: group 13 selectors 34+35 (read), 46+47 (write)
    a6xx:        group 13 selector 63 (read), 84 (write)

Selector names for a7xx come from Mesa's public register description
(src/freedreno/registers/adreno/a7xx_perfcntrs.xml):
PERF_GBIF_AXI0/1_READ_DATA_BEATS_TOTAL and ..._WRITE_DATA_BEATS_TOTAL.
One data beat is 32 bytes.

The helper source is in src/gpu_counters.c and can be rebuilt with:

    zig cc -target aarch64-linux-musl -static -O2 -s -o gpu_counters \
        src/gpu_counters.c
